# Force LF on all checkouts. Authoring on Windows must NOT introduce CRLF into the
# s6 run scripts: a trailing \r turns "#!/usr/bin/with-contenv bash" into an invalid
# interpreter path and the service silently fails to start. The same goes for the files
# the Dockerfile reads at build time (packages.txt, debconf-selections, the apt pin): a CR
# would end up inside a package name or a debconf answer.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
root/** text eol=lf
# The template icon is binary; never let a text filter touch it.
*.png binary
